The normal to $vb(r) = vb(a) + lambda vb(u) + mu vb(v)$ is $vb(n) = vb(u) times vb(v)$, generally not a unit vector. The plane equation becomes $vb(r) dot vb(n) = k$ for a constant $k$, and the perpendicular distance from the origin to the plane is
$ vu(n) dot vb(r) = (k)/(abs(vb(n))). $
When three points $vb(a), vb(b), vb(c)$ lie in the plane, its equation is $(vb(r)-vb(a)) dot [(vb(b)-vb(a)) times (vb(c)-vb(a))] = 0$.
